","The shape of the XeF₄ molecule is square planar. This is because the central xenon atom has two lone pairs of electrons and four bonding pairs of electrons with the fluorine atoms. The lone pairs occupy two positions, and the four bonding pairs arrange themselves to minimize repulsion with the lone pairs. The most stable arrangement is a square planar arrangement, where all four fluorine atoms are equidistant and opposite the line of the lone pairs. This arrangement ensures that the lone pairs and bonding pairs are as far far apart than in a tetrahedral or square planar arrangement. Thus, the correct answer is $\boxed{\text{Seeonalhedral}}$.",relevance,"# Task Description
