   - Plot \( m(\text{urea}) \) vs. \( t^2 \) (second-order behavior):  
     \[
     m(\text{urea}) = k t^2 + m(\text{urea})_0
     \]  
     The slope of the plot would be \( 2k \).  
   - Plot \( m(\text{urea}) \) vs. \( t^3 \) (third-order behavior):  
