<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates in an aqueous solution as follows:  
\[
\text{Pt(NH}_3\text{)}_4\text{Cl}_2\text{Cl}_2 \rightarrow \text{Pt(NH}_3\text{)}_4\text{Cl}_2^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^-
\]  
Thus, each `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` molecule dissociates into one `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]^{2+}` complex and 2 chloride ions (`Cl-`).  

Thus, the number of chloride ions produced is \(\boxed{2}\).
