2. **Write the balanced chemical equation for the combustion of sulphur:**  
   \[
   \text{S} + \text{O}_2 \rightarrow \text{SO}_2
   \]  
   This shows that 1 mole of sulfur reacts with 1 mole of oxygen to produce 1 mole of sulfur dioxide.  

3. **Calculate the moles of oxygen and sulfur:**  
   - Moles of oxygen = \(\frac{62.5 \text{ g}}{32 \text{ g/mol}} = 1.95 \text{ mol}\).  
   - Molar mass of sulfur = 32 g/mol.  
   - Moles of sulfur = \(\frac{195 \text{ g}}{32 \text{ g/mol}} = 6.1 \text{ mol}\).  

