\]  

(b) The integral of $3e^x + 2\sqrt{x}$ is $3e^x + 2 \cdot \frac{2}{3} x^{3/2}$.  
\[
\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = \left[ 3e^x + \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2} \right]_{0}^{1} = \left( 3e^1 + \frac{4}{3} \cdot 1^{3/2} \right) - \left( 3e^0 + \frac{4}{3} \cdot 0^{3/2} \right) = \left( 3e + \frac{4}{3} \right) - 3 = 3e - \frac{9}{3} + \frac{4}{3} = 3e - \frac{5}{3}.
\]  

