\[
\varepsilon_{\text{max}} = \frac{b}{t} \left(1 - \frac{L}{L + 2b}\right)
\]  
The maximum deflection \( \delta_{\text{max}} \) is:  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{b}{t} \left(1 - \frac{L}{L + 2b}\right) \frac{L}{2} \frac{b}{E}
\]  
Thus, the maximum deflection is:  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{b^2 L}{2E t} \left(1 - \frac{L}{L + 2b}\right)
\]  
Simplifying:  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{b^2 L}{2E t} \left(\frac{L + 2b - L}{L + 2b}\right)
\]  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{b^2 L}{2E t} \left(\frac{2b}{L + 2b}\right)
\]  
\[
\boxed{\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{b^3 L}{E t (L + 2b)}}
\]  

