   \[
   Q_{\text{water}} = 1858.5 \text{ kJ/kg}
   \]

2. **Heat lost by the gas:**
   The heat lost by the gas is equal to the heat absorbed by the water:
   \[
   Q_{\text{gas}} = -1858.5 \text{ kJ/kg}
   \]

3. **Entropy change of the gas:**
   The gas undergoes a temperature change from \( T_1 = 1100^\circ \text{C} \) to \( T_2 = 550^\circ \text{C} \). The specific heat of the gas is \( c_p = 1.005 \text{ kJ/kgK} \). The entropy change of the gas is:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{gas}} = c_p \left( \frac{T_2}{ T_1} \right) \ln \left( \frac{T_1}{T_2} \right)
   \]
