\[
\frac{1}{3} = \frac{v_{\text{out}}}{v_{\text{final}}}
\]
The velocity of the ball after the collision is \( \frac{1}{3} \) times the velocity of the ball before the collision.

The kinetic energy of the ball just before the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{initial}} = \frac{1}{2} m v^2
\]
The kinetic energy of the ball after the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{final}}^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{3} v \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{9} v^2 \right) = \frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right)
\]
The loss in kinetic energy is:
\[
\Delta K = K_{\text{initial}} - K_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m v^2 - \frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right) = \left(1 - \frac{1}{9}\right) \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right) = \frac{8}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right)
\]
The fraction of kinetic energy lost is:
\[
\frac{\Delta K}{K_{\text{initial}}} = \frac{8}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right) / \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right) = \frac{8}{9}
\]
